[IQ Generator Preset]
# Lesson 12: minimum-shift keying.
# MSK is binary FSK with the smallest tone spacing that keeps the two tones orthogonal over one symbol: h = 0.5, so the tones sit at plus and minus symbol rate / 4 (250 Hz here). The phase moves exactly plus or minus 90 degrees per symbol. Compare the Spectrum tab with lesson 11: the closer tones give a much narrower main lobe at the same bit rate. MSK ignores the tone spacing setting.
